<title>THAILAND: Hantex says employee action stops output.</title>
<headline>Hantex says employee action stops output.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai textile manufacturer Hantex Plc said on Thursday an employee rally at its factory in Samut Sakhon caused it to stop production on January 8.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement to the Stock Exchange of Thailand that the work stoppage would cost about one million baht ($40,000) a day.</p>
<p>THe company said there were 500 employees in the factory and only 95 have reported to work. It said it has tried to negotiate with employees but failed to work out a solution so will proceed with legal action.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Hantex shares were untraded in the first half hour of dealings. They closed at 9.30 baht on Thursday. ($1 = 25 baht) -- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
